      "body": "The shared dropdown-menu-content sizes its width to the anchor (`w-(--bits-dropdown-menu-anchor-width)`) floored at `min-w-32` (128px) — fine for the wide select-style menus that rely on it (e.g. the diff-theme picker), but the comment menu anchors a tiny ••• button, so \"View on GitHub\" wrapped to two lines at 128px. Fixed locally with `w-auto!` so this menu sizes to its content instead. Used the important modifier because tailwind-merge v2.6 doesn't recognise the v4 `w-(...)` arbitrary-property syntax as conflicting, so a plain `w-auto` wouldn't reliably win. Verified in a faithful absolute-positioned repro: before = 128px / two lines, after = ~145px / one line.",
